From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:07:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: MutationObserver delivers records

observe, disconnect and takeRecords were stubs, so a callback never ran.
observe() now registers the node with its options (childList, attributes,
characterData, subtree, attributeOldValue, characterDataOldValue,
attributeFilter) on the document; the document observer of the Gecko engine
queues a record for every observer that is interested, and the callback gets
an array of MutationRecord objects (type, target, addedNodes, removedNodes,
previousSibling, nextSibling, attributeName, attributeNamespace, oldValue) and
the observer, after the script that made the change has finished. The old
value of an attribute or text is taken before the change. A node observed
twice replaces its options. Records are plain script arrays for the node lists.

diff --git a/dlls/mshtml/htmlscript.h b/dlls/mshtml/htmlscript.h
index c1b1aa2..c47751c 100644
--- a/dlls/mshtml/htmlscript.h
+++ b/dlls/mshtml/htmlscript.h
@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@ void connect_scripts(HTMLInnerWindow*);
 void doc_insert_script(HTMLInnerWindow*,HTMLScriptElement*,BOOL);
 IDispatch *script_parse_event(HTMLInnerWindow*,LPCWSTR);
 HRESULT exec_script(HTMLInnerWindow*,const WCHAR*,const WCHAR*,VARIANT*);
+HRESULT exec_script_expr(HTMLInnerWindow*,const WCHAR*,VARIANT*);
 void update_browser_script_mode(GeckoBrowser*,IUri*);
 BOOL find_global_prop(HTMLInnerWindow*,const WCHAR*,DWORD,ScriptHost**,DISPID*);
